From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shaurizard <contact@nyoom.engineering>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 51/51] feat(gpu): give 8x host render targets the alpha to
 coverage of 4x

Xenos MSAA is at most 4x, but a host renderer may draw a guest surface
into a render target of more samples than the guest's, such as 8x for
better antialiasing. Such a renderer sets sample_count_log2 to 4x's, and
on the RTV path the alpha to coverage mask of the 4x case covers only
samples 0:3 of the eight.

On the RTV path, the 4x case now also copies the coverage of samples 0:3
to 4:7, so that each of the four dithered thresholds covers two of the
eight samples and a coverage of n/4 of the pixel stays n/4. Direct3D
ignores the output coverage bits of samples a render target does not
have, so 4x targets are unaffected. The ROV path, which keeps its own
coverage and deferred depth/stencil bits, is unchanged.

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/src/graphics/pipeline/shader/dxbc_translator_om.cpp b/src/graphics/pipeline/shader/dxbc_translator_om.cpp
--- a/src/graphics/pipeline/shader/dxbc_translator_om.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/pipeline/shader/dxbc_translator_om.cpp
@@ -1786,6 +1786,13 @@ void DxbcShaderTranslator::CompletePixelShader_AlphaToMask() {
                                           coverage_temp_component, temp, 1);
     CompletePixelShader_AlphaToMaskSample(false, 3, 1.0f, temp_x_src, 1.0f / 16.0f, coverage_temp,
                                           coverage_temp_component, temp, 1);
+    if (!edram_rov_used_) {
+      // For a host target of 8 samples (more than the guest's 4), each threshold covers two:
+      // samples 4:7 get the coverage of 0:3. A 4-sample target ignores the bits above 3.
+      a_.OpBFI(dxbc::Dest::R(coverage_temp, 1 << coverage_temp_component), dxbc::Src::LU(4),
+               dxbc::Src::LU(4), dxbc::Src::R(coverage_temp).Select(coverage_temp_component),
+               dxbc::Src::R(coverage_temp).Select(coverage_temp_component));
+    }
     // 2x MSAA.
     // With ROV, using guest sample indices.
     // Without ROV:
